# What makes this package an add-on (docs/src/content/docs/addons.md). One
# capability. ADDON_FEATURE: the console's Backhaul > Cellular, the cellular
# endpoints and the Overview card, there while this is installed.
ADDON_TITLE="Cellular"
ADDON_CAPS="cellular"
ADDON_FEATURE="cellular"
# Built in where the modem is soldered to the board (PULZR_ADDONS_BUILTIN on
# the RAK7268C, RAK7268CV2 and RAK7289CV2: their one USB host port is the
# modem's, and it is QMI). Installed on request where the modem is whatever is
# plugged into a USB host port: the Opal, the Pis and the RAK7391, whose LTE
# is an optional mPCIe card on USB. pulzr-radios reports a modem plugged into
# one of those (`modems`), and Pulzar Net offers this add-on for it. A board
# with neither gets no cellular at all.
ADDON_BOARDS="gl-sft1200 rpi3 rpi4 rpi5 rak7391 rak7268c rak7268cv2 rak7289cv2"
# The gateway's backhaul may be this add-on alone (a SIM, no cable), and a
# gateway that upgrades without it has nothing to download it back over. So
# pulzr-addon carry fetches the next release's build of it before an upgrade,
# and it is put back from that copy on the first boot, before the firmware is
# judged (pulzr-addon, "CARRIED ACROSS AN UPGRADE").
ADDON_CARRY="1"
